I_Error: the exit functions first, then the message; no zenity.

The terminal frontend draws on the alternate screen with the terminal in raw mode, and gives the
terminal back in an exit function: printed before that, I_Error's message vanished with the
alternate screen. The exit functions (those for errors) now run first, the message after them. The
GUI error box (zenity through system()) is not tried: the message is on the terminal.

diff --git a/doomgeneric/i_system.c b/doomgeneric/i_system.c
index 53ab2c9..c8f53e6 100644
--- a/doomgeneric/i_system.c
+++ b/doomgeneric/i_system.c
@@ -375,6 +375,20 @@ void I_Error (char *error, ...)
         already_quitting = true;
     }
 
+    // doomterm: the exit functions first: they give the terminal back (the game drew on the
+    // alternate screen), so that the message is seen where the game was run.
+    entry = exit_funcs;
+
+    while (entry != NULL)
+    {
+        if (entry->run_on_error)
+        {
+            entry->func();
+        }
+
+        entry = entry->next;
+    }
+
     // Message first.
     va_start(argptr, error);
     //fprintf(stderr, "\nError: ");
@@ -389,21 +403,9 @@ void I_Error (char *error, ...)
     M_vsnprintf(msgbuf, sizeof(msgbuf), error, argptr);
     va_end(argptr);
 
-    // Shutdown. Here might be other errors.
-
-    entry = exit_funcs;
-
-    while (entry != NULL)
-    {
-        if (entry->run_on_error)
-        {
-            entry->func();
-        }
-
-        entry = entry->next;
-    }
+    // (doomterm: the exit functions ran above)
 
-    exit_gui_popup = !M_ParmExists("-nogui");
+    exit_gui_popup = 0;  // doomterm: no zenity; the message is on the terminal
 
     // Pop up a GUI dialog box to show the error message, if the
     // game was not run from the console (and the user will
